### Snapshot and verify the script tree without blocking cancellation

**Severity:** `high`

Directory enumeration, copying, hashing, and metadata reads currently run synchronously in the execution path. Move the complete snapshot operation to cancellable background work.

```suggestion
            var metadata = await Task.Run(
                () =>
                {
                    foreach (var sourceFile in System.IO.Directory.EnumerateFiles(scriptRoot, "*.py", System.IO.SearchOption.AllDirectories))
                    {
                        cancellationToken.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();
                        var destinationFile = System.IO.Path.Combine(snapshotDirectory, System.IO.Path.GetRelativePath(scriptRoot, sourceFile));
                        System.IO.Directory.CreateDirectory(System.IO.Path.GetDirectoryName(destinationFile)!);
                        System.IO.File.Copy(sourceFile, destinationFile);
                    }

                    if (!string.Equals(_pythonScriptTrustService.ComputeHash(snapshotScriptPath), trustedHash, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
                    {
                        throw new InvalidOperationException("The Python script changed while it was being prepared for execution. Please try again.");
                    }

                    return _pythonScriptService.ReadMetadata(snapshotScriptPath);
                },
                cancellationToken);
```

### Preserve the generic file format during execution

**Severity:** `high`

The eligibility path treats storage items as files, but execution recomputes the formats without that adjustment. Restore the File flag so an eligible files action receives a matching payload.

```suggestion
            var detectedFormat = await clipboardData.GetAvailableFormatsAsync();
            if (clipboardData.Contains(StandardDataFormats.StorageItems))
            {
                detectedFormat |= ClipboardFormat.File;
            }
```

### Repair and persist null nested Python settings during migration

**Severity:** `high`

Legacy JSON may explicitly contain null Windows or WSL settings. Initialize both objects, preserve the legacy folder choice, and return whether repairs must be saved.

```suggestion
    public bool MigrateLegacyIfNeeded()
    {
        bool repairedNestedSettings = WindowsSettings is null || WslSettings is null;
        WindowsSettings ??= new();
        WslSettings ??= new();

        bool changed = repairedNestedSettings ||
                       IsEnabled.HasValue ||
                       UseWsl.HasValue ||
                       ScriptsFolder is not null ||
                       PythonExecutablePath is not null ||
                       WslDistribution is not null;

        // Only migrate if Mode hasn't been set by the new UI yet
        // (i.e., still at default "disabled") AND legacy fields are present.
        if (IsEnabled.HasValue && string.Equals(Mode, "disabled", System.StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
        {
            // Migrate from old format
            if (!IsEnabled.Value)
            {
                Mode = "disabled";
            }
            else if (UseWsl == true)
            {
                Mode = "wsl";
            }
            else
            {
                Mode = "windows";
            }

            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(ScriptsFolder))
            {
                if (UseWsl == true)
                {
                    WslSettings.ScriptsFolder = ScriptsFolder;
                }
                else
                {
                    WindowsSettings.ScriptsFolder = ScriptsFolder;
                }
            }

            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(PythonExecutablePath))
            {
                WindowsSettings.PythonExecutablePath = PythonExecutablePath;
            }

            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(WslDistribution))
            {
                WslSettings.Distribution = WslDistribution;
            }
        }

        // Always clear legacy fields so they don't persist
        IsEnabled = null;
        UseWsl = null;
        ScriptsFolder = null;
        PythonExecutablePath = null;
        WslDistribution = null;

        return changed;
```

### Persist trusted hashes outside the UI thread

**Severity:** `high`

The synchronous lock can deadlock against settings reload. Run the locked file update on background work and return a task to the caller.

```suggestion
        public Task StoreTrustedScriptHashAsync(string scriptPath, string hash)
        {
            return Task.Run(() =>
            {
                lock (_loadingSettingsLock)
                {
                    try
                    {
                        var settings = _settingsUtils.GetSettingsOrDefault<AdvancedPasteSettings>(AdvancedPasteModuleName);
                        if (settings?.Properties?.PythonScripts is null)
                        {
                            return;
                        }

                        settings.Properties.PythonScripts.TrustedScriptHashes ??= new Dictionary<string, string>();
                        settings.Properties.PythonScripts.TrustedScriptHashes[scriptPath] = hash;
                        settings.Save(_settingsUtils);

                        // Update in-memory cache.
                        var updated = new Dictionary<string, string>(TrustedScriptHashes, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                        {
                            [scriptPath] = hash,
                        };
                        TrustedScriptHashes = updated;
                    }
                    catch (Exception ex)
                    {
                        Logger.LogError("Failed to store trusted script hash", ex);
                    }
                }
            });
```

### Forward trust persistence asynchronously

**Severity:** `high`

Return the settings task instead of synchronously writing the trusted hash.

```suggestion
    public Task StoreTrustAsync(string scriptPath, string hash)
    {
        return _userSettings.StoreTrustedScriptHashAsync(scriptPath, hash);
```

### Terminate Windows import probes on cancellation

**Severity:** `high`

User cancellation currently escapes while leaving the Python probe running. Kill the complete process tree before propagating cancellation.

```suggestion
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException)
        {
            process.Kill(entireProcessTree: true);
            throw;
        }
```

